# tally 2.1.8 item 77 (#201), E §4.1 step 2 and L §4.4: a test of a window-dated movement that comes out one way on
# some of its days and another on the rest is the window's hole, as far as the refusal or the other class would reach.
# empty moves tmp's 100.00 PLN to jar on a day of window(03-05, 03-10); tmp's lifespan ends on 03-07. Moved on 03-05 to
# 03-07, tmp ends empty and jar holds 100.00 PLN; on 03-08 to 03-10 the leg is outside tmp's lifespan and tmp ends
# holding 100.00 PLN. e1 and e3 are the hole, and each splits. 2.1.7's refcore refused both (RUN-LIFESPAN). The plan's
# i77a e1 and e3.
# tally 2.2 (2.2-4): the clause `windows each` is cut; its asks are the plain line, the hole with each unknown day it
# carries named (`unknown day:`, 2.2-11). A caller who takes the window as one day pins its cell.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-06-30

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
kind accts: place PLN signed
kind pots: place PLN min 0
place jar: accts lives 2025-01-01..
place tmp: accts lives 2025-01-01..2026-03-07
place pot: pots lives 2025-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input amt: money PLN
input wd: date
input wa: date
input wb: date

move empty: transfers
  on wd
  leg cash from tmp to jar amount amt

move oa: transfers
  on wa
  leg cash from pot to world amount amt

move ob: transfers
  on wb
  leg cash from world to pot amount amt

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2025-12-01
  amt = 100.00 PLN "s"
  wd = window(2026-03-05, 2026-03-10) "s"
  wa = window(2026-04-05, 2026-04-10) "s"
  wb = window(2026-04-07, 2026-04-12) "s"
  opening[jar] = 0.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "s"
  opening[tmp] = 100.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "s"
  opening[pot] = 50.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "s"

ask e1: bal(jar, 2026-03-31)
ask e2: bal(jar, 2026-03-31)
ask e3: bal(tmp, 2026-03-07)
ask e4: bal(tmp, 2026-03-07)
=== expect
e1: ?"date within window(2026-03-05, 2026-03-10) not precise enough for a balance" (empty)
  unknown day: wd
  cut 2026-01-01
e2: ?"date within window(2026-03-05, 2026-03-10) not precise enough for a balance" (empty)
  unknown day: wd
  cut 2026-01-01
e3: ?"date within window(2026-03-05, 2026-03-10) not precise enough for a balance" (empty)
  unknown day: wd
  cut 2026-01-01
e4: ?"date within window(2026-03-05, 2026-03-10) not precise enough for a balance" (empty)
  unknown day: wd
  cut 2026-01-01
